<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n440" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcerbo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		id. (vox Vergil.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To make harsh</i> or <i>bitter</i>,
				<i>to embitter;</i> lit. and trop. (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gaudia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 12, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 655</span></i>
			.— Hence in an extended sense, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To augment</i> or <i>aggravate any
				thing disagreeable</i> (cf. acuo): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formidine crimen acerbat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 407</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nefas Eteoclis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 214</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
